{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$ is the *second derivative* of $y$. In other words, it's the derivative of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$, which is the derivative of $y$.\n\nBecause of this, we need to differentiate $y$ twice in order to find $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[5\\cos(2x+10)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-10\\sin(2x+10)\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[5\\cos(2x+10)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5[-\\sin(2x+10)]\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}(2x+10)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-5\\sin(2x+10)\\cdot 2\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-10\\sin(2x+10)\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Now we can differentiate $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ to find $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-10\\sin(2x+10)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-20\\cos(2x+10)\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-10\\sin(2x+10)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-10\\cos(2x+10)\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}(2x+10)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-10\\cos(2x+10)\\cdot 2\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-20\\cos(2x+10)\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=-20\\cos(2x+10)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $y=5\\cos(2x+10)$.\n\n**Find $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$.**\n\n$\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"-20\\cos(2x+10)"}],"buttonSets":["basic","trig","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
